Work around nvcc rejecting exec::async_scope::on_empty().

on_empty() is a non-template constexpr member with a deduced return type
whose body calls just(). nvcc 12.9 hands it to the gcc 12 host compiler in a
form where just() is a void expression, so every translation unit compiled by
nvcc that includes exec/async_scope.hpp fails, whether or not on_empty() is
used. Under nvcc, make on_empty() a member template so its body is only
instantiated when it is called; callers keep writing scope.on_empty().
Other compilers are unchanged.

Keep this separate from the other nvcc patches so an existing FetchContent
checkout with those workarounds already applied can acquire this fix too.

See TheHPXProject/hpx#7676 and NVIDIA/stdexec#2304.

